  "title": "SPEC-MAT-002D — Material Consumption, Return, Adjustment, Destruction & Reconciliation Events",
  "description": "Document 113 event contract for the events app/modules/material/commands.py actually emits for Document 22. 8 of the catalogue's 9 declared events are implemented: MaterialConsumed, MaterialReturned, MaterialSampled, MaterialLossRecorded (mutually exclusive outcomes of the same loss-recording call site, chosen by loss_type), InventoryAdjustmentApproved, MaterialDestroyed, MaterialReconciliationCalculated, MaterialReconciliationFailed (mutually exclusive outcomes of the same reconciliation call site, chosen by outcome). ERPInventoryPostingFailed is declared but has no producing code path -- ERP posting-failure handling is not yet built on the material side. Verified directly against source. KNOWN DEFECT (SG-174, not fixed here): app/modules/yield_reconciliation/commands.py also emits the literal event_type \"MaterialReconciliationCalculated\" (Document 17 batch material reconciliation, aggregate_type reconciliation_record) -- a second, independent cross-module name collision, same class as LineClearanceCompleted. tooling/events/validate.py correctly fails CTRC-FR-008 on this pair too; left standing as accurate evidence.",
